Engineering Geology Field Manual — U.S. Bureau of Reclamation (@mine-fieldmanual: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mine-sources) { r_5WS5PNK19008B3SV6D1WWNVTRE
U.S. Bureau of Reclamation, Technical Service Center. Engineering Geology Field Manual, volumes I and II. [Official complete volumes and chapter downloads](https://www.usbr.gov/tsc/techreferences/mands/geologyfieldmanual.html).

Read volume I in full for material description, discontinuities, mapping, surveys, drilling, groundwater, logs, and investigation records. Read the complete volume-II methods used in the study, including permeability/water observations, sampling/core handling, and surveying. Identify the actual edition/chapter date and purpose rather than treating historical guidance as a current universal design code.

The official contents and authorized complete/individual downloads were accessible on 29 October 2026. Preserve agency and component notices. The manual supports field/method studies; actual operating competence requires appropriate facilities and guidance. No volume, image, or external observation collection is bundled.

